  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "Dilution",
      "excerpt": "DILUTION The\ndifference between the public offering price per share and the net tangible book value (\u201cNTBV\u201d) per ordinary share after\nthis offering constitutes the dilution to investors in this offering. NTBV per share is determined by dividing our NTBV, which is\nour total tangible assets less total liabilities (including the value of ordinary shares that may be redeemed for cash), by the\nnumber of outstanding ordinary shares. The following table gives effect to the limitation under our restated and amended memorandum\nand articles of association that will prohibit redemptions in an amount that would cause our net tangible assets to be less than\n$5,000,001. As\nof September 30, 2026 our net tangible book value deficit was $244,066, or approximately $0.09 per share. For the\npurposes of the dilution calculation, in order to present the maximum estimated dilution as a result of this offering,",
      "status": "source_excerpt_not_model_conclusion"
    }
  ],
